WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.333 --> 00:00:14.674
months had passed since Mr.

2
00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:15.815
Bumble had married Mrs.

3
00:00:15.875 --> 00:00:17.657
Corney, the matron of the workhouse.

4
00:00:18.738 --> 00:00:21.881
Mr. Bumble had become the master of the workhouse, but he was unhappy.

5
00:00:22.821 --> 00:00:26.845
He no longer wore the gold-lace trimmed coat and the cocked hat of the parish officer.

6
00:00:27.846 --> 00:00:29.767
And he quarreled constantly with the new Mrs.

7
00:00:29.828 --> 00:00:36.341
Bumble. "I was misled by six teaspoons, a pair of sugar tongs, a small quantity of secondhand furniture,

8
00:00:36.462 --> 00:00:38.242
and twenty pounds in cash," Mr.

9
00:00:38.282 --> 00:00:39.282
Bumble said to himself.

10
00:00:39.302 --> 00:00:43.263
"We've been married only a short time, but it seems like forever."

11
00:00:44.284 --> 00:00:46.284
He had just had another argument with his wife.

12
00:00:47.424 --> 00:00:49.905
Snatching up his hat, he left the workhouse in a hurry.

13
00:00:50.945 --> 00:00:53.206
He roamed the streets until it began to rain heavily.

14
00:00:54.166 --> 00:00:55.567
Then he stepped inside a pub.

15
00:00:56.627 --> 00:00:59.968
Mr. Bumble went into the parlor to enjoy his drink and read the newspaper.

16
00:01:01.644 --> 00:01:05.946
There was only one other person sitting at the table: a tall man, wearing a dark cloak.

17
00:01:06.986 --> 00:01:09.988
The man's clothes were dusty, as if he'd traveled a great distance.

18
00:01:11.088 --> 00:01:11.448
As Mr.

19
00:01:11.488 --> 00:01:14.750
Bumble read the newspaper, he couldn't resist stealing a look at the stranger.

20
00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:18.392
And every time he did, the stranger was looking at him!

21
00:01:19.492 --> 00:01:22.213
Finally the man said, "I think I've seen you before.

22
00:01:23.174 --> 00:01:24.954
You used to be the parish officer, didn't you?"

23
00:01:24.974 --> 00:01:27.195
"Yes," said Mr.

24
00:01:27.215 --> 00:01:28.056
Bumble in surprise.

25
00:01:29.152 --> 00:01:32.074
The stranger stood up and closed the door so no one would overhear him.

26
00:01:32.094 --> 00:01:34.716
"I came to this place today to find you.

27
00:01:35.717 --> 00:01:37.918
I want some information, and I'm willing to pay for it."

28
00:01:38.919 --> 00:01:40.580
He pushed some coins across the table.

29
00:01:41.561 --> 00:01:45.303
The master of the workhouse carefully examined the coins to be sure that they were genuine.

30
00:01:46.264 --> 00:01:47.485
Then he put them in his pocket.

31
00:01:47.505 --> 00:01:53.269
"Cast your mind back to the workhouse about ten or twelve years ago," said the stranger.

32
00:01:53.289 --> 00:01:55.710
"A boy was born there one night."

33
00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:57.672
"Many boys were.

34
00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:00.601
How can you expect me to remember just one?"

35
00:02:00.621 --> 00:02:05.565
"I'm talking about a meek-looking, pale boy, who was apprenticed to an undertaker.

36
00:02:06.625 --> 00:02:07.966
He later ran away to London."

37
00:02:09.007 --> 00:02:10.828
"Why, you mean Oliver Twist!"

38
00:02:11.209 --> 00:02:11.609
said Mr.

39
00:02:11.629 --> 00:02:14.251
Bumble. "I remember him, of course.

40
00:02:15.271 --> 00:02:20.715
There wasn't a worse rascal in the work—" "I don't want to hear about him," interrupted the stranger.

41
00:02:20.735 --> 00:02:22.696
"I've heard enough of him.

42
00:02:23.777 --> 00:02:26.279
I want to know about the old woman who took care of his mother.

43
00:02:27.339 --> 00:02:27.960
Where is she?"

44
00:02:28.888 --> 00:02:31.169
"You're talking about old Sally," said Mr.

45
00:02:31.209 --> 00:02:33.850
Bumble. "She died last winter."

46
00:02:34.931 --> 00:02:37.192
The stranger sat lost in thought for a few minutes.

47
00:02:38.272 --> 00:02:40.873
Mr. Bumble couldn't tell if he was relieved or disappointed.

48
00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:44.755
"It doesn't matter," the stranger said at last.

49
00:02:45.876 --> 00:02:47.556
With that, he rose as if to depart.

50
00:02:48.577 --> 00:02:48.977
But Mr.

51
00:02:48.997 --> 00:02:51.258
Bumble saw an opportunity to make some more money.

52
00:02:52.278 --> 00:02:55.560
He remembered how agitated his wife had been on the night that Sally died.

53
00:02:56.712 --> 00:02:58.754
Although he didn't know everything Sally had told Mrs.

54
00:02:58.794 --> 00:03:00.575
Bumble, he knew it concerned Oliver.

55
00:03:00.595 --> 00:03:04.458
"There's one woman who might be able to help you," he said.

56
00:03:05.499 --> 00:03:07.300
The stranger's face seemed to fill with fear.

57
00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.261
"How can I find her?"

58
00:03:10.222 --> 00:03:11.403
"You'll have to go through me."

59
00:03:12.324 --> 00:03:15.686
The stranger wrote out an address on a scrap of paper and handed it to Mr.

60
00:03:15.726 --> 00:03:18.869
Bumble. "Bring her to me tomorrow night at nine o'clock."

61
00:03:19.969 --> 00:03:23.072
After that the two men left the pub, heading in opposite directions.

62
00:03:24.128 --> 00:03:24.528
But Mr.

63
00:03:24.548 --> 00:03:28.912
Bumble soon realized he needed one more piece of information and hurried after the stranger.

64
00:03:28.932 --> 00:03:31.453
"What do you want?"

65
00:03:31.854 --> 00:03:33.195
cried the man, whirling around.

66
00:03:33.215 --> 00:03:36.157
"What name am I to ask for tomorrow night?"

67
00:03:37.258 --> 00:03:40.220
"Monks!" The man strode hastily away.

68
00:03:41.301 --> 00:03:43.422
The sky was dull and overcast when Mr.

69
00:03:43.462 --> 00:03:43.802
and Mrs.

70
00:03:43.842 --> 00:03:45.163
Bumble set out the next night.

71
00:03:46.224 --> 00:03:50.727
The clouds, which had been threatening all day, were spread out densely, as if preparing for a violent

72
00:03:50.827 --> 00:03:56.411
thunderstorm. The Bumbles were both wrapped in shabby outer garments that would protect them from the rain and

73
00:03:56.451 --> 00:03:57.832
keep them from being recognized.

74
00:03:58.853 --> 00:04:01.696
They headed toward some run-down houses bordering the river.

75
00:04:02.696 --> 00:04:05.739
The people who lived there survived by theft and other crimes.

76
00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:09.142
Among these houses stood an old factory building.

77
00:04:09.162 --> 00:04:11.984
"This should be the place," said Mr.

78
00:04:12.024 --> 00:04:14.226
Bumble, consulting the scrap of paper in his hand.

79
00:04:14.246 --> 00:04:17.608
"Hello!" cried a voice from above.

80
00:04:17.628 --> 00:04:19.630
"I'll be down in a minute."

81
00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:21.632
"Is that the man?"

82
00:04:21.984 --> 00:04:22.884
Mrs. Bumble asked.

83
00:04:23.945 --> 00:04:24.745
Her husband nodded.

84
00:04:24.765 --> 00:04:28.687
"Then say as little as you can until we find out what he wants."

85
00:04:29.987 --> 00:04:33.709
Monks opened the door, motioned for them to come in quickly, and then shut the door.

86
00:04:33.729 --> 00:04:35.570
"Is this the woman?"

87
00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:39.351
Mr. Bumble only nodded, remembering his wife's warning.

88
00:04:40.411 --> 00:04:41.972
Suddenly there was a crack of thunder.

89
00:04:43.053 --> 00:04:44.633
Monks turned away for a few minutes.

90
00:04:45.814 --> 00:04:48.995
When he looked at them again, his face was distorted and discolored.

91
00:04:49.015 --> 00:04:52.240
"These fits come over me now and then," he said.

92
00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:54.662
"Thunder sometimes brings them on."

93
00:04:55.802 --> 00:04:57.143
A lantern cast a dim light.

94
00:04:58.224 --> 00:04:59.764
Monks motioned for them to sit down.

95
00:05:00.825 --> 00:05:03.186
Mr. Bumble looked nervously around, but Mrs.

96
00:05:03.226 --> 00:05:04.027
Bumble was calm.

97
00:05:04.047 --> 00:05:07.789
"Let's get down to business," Monks said to Mrs.

98
00:05:07.849 --> 00:05:11.170
Bumble. "Were you with Oliver's mother the night she died?"

99
00:05:11.191 --> 00:05:14.993
"Yes." "Something was taken from her.

100
00:05:16.053 --> 00:05:19.655
Something that she wore "What's the information worth to you?"

101
00:05:20.055 --> 00:05:21.096
Mrs. Bumble interrupted.

102
00:05:22.208 --> 00:05:24.550
"It could be twenty pounds; it could be nothing."

103
00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:26.831
"I know I have what you want.

104
00:05:27.892 --> 00:05:29.213
Make it twenty-five pounds."

105
00:05:30.214 --> 00:05:32.095
"Twenty-five?" Monks pulled away.

106
00:05:32.115 --> 00:05:34.637
"What if your information is useless?"

107
00:05:34.657 --> 00:05:37.439
"You can easily take the money from me.

108
00:05:38.519 --> 00:05:40.120
I'm alone and unprotected here."

109
00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:43.903
"Not alone, my dear, nor unprotected," Mr.

110
00:05:43.923 --> 00:05:45.824
Bumble said in a voice trembling with fear.

111
00:05:46.985 --> 00:05:50.728
Monks removed a canvas bag from his pocket and laid twenty-five pounds on the table.

112
00:05:51.796 --> 00:05:53.196
Mrs. Bumble began her story.

113
00:05:53.216 --> 00:05:57.898
"Sally told me she stole a gold necklace from Oliver's mother.

114
00:05:58.978 --> 00:06:02.479
She sold it to a pawn shop, but she told me where to find the pawn ticket.

115
00:06:03.679 --> 00:06:05.800
I redeemed the necklace, and here it is."

116
00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:08.621
Mrs. Bumble held out a gold locket.

117
00:06:09.661 --> 00:06:11.562
Monks pried it open with trembling hands.

118
00:06:12.742 --> 00:06:15.103
Inside were two locks of hair and a wedding ring.

119
00:06:16.163 --> 00:06:19.924
The locket was inscribed Agnes, with space left for a last name.

120
00:06:20.972 --> 00:06:24.754
There was also a date, which was about a year before Oliver was born.

121
00:06:24.774 --> 00:06:27.456
"Is this what you wanted from me?"

122
00:06:27.856 --> 00:06:28.276
asked Mrs.

123
00:06:28.336 --> 00:06:31.098
Bumble. "It is," said Monks.

124
00:06:31.118 --> 00:06:34.760
"And now I must destroy this evidence of Oliver's past."

125
00:06:35.841 --> 00:06:39.543
He suddenly wheeled the table aside and pulled up a trapdoor in the floor.

126
00:06:40.564 --> 00:06:43.405
The three of them looked down at the river swirling angrily below.

127
00:06:44.546 --> 00:06:47.788
Monks took a deep breath and then threw the locket into the river.
